---@field enterpriseId? string The ID of the enterprise for which the notification is sent. This will always be present.
---@field appRestrictionsSchemaChangeEvent? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.AppRestrictionsSchemaChangeEvent Notifications about new app restrictions schema changes.
---@field newPermissionsEvent? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.NewPermissionsEvent Notifications about new app permissions.
---@field timestampMillis? string The time when the notification was published in milliseconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z. This will always be present.
---@field deviceReportUpdateEvent? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.DeviceReportUpdateEvent Notifications about device report updates.
---@field productApprovalEvent? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductApprovalEvent Notifications about changes to a product's approval status.
---@field newDeviceEvent? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.NewDeviceEvent Notifications about new devices.
---@field notificationType? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.NotificationNotificationTypeEnum Type of the notification.
---@field appUpdateEvent? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.AppUpdateEvent Notifications about app updates.
---@field installFailureEvent? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.InstallFailureEvent Notifications about an app installation failure.

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.NotificationList gcp.androidenterprise_v1.Notification[]

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.NotificationNotificationTypeEnum "unknown"|"testNotification"|"productApproval"|"installFailure"|"appUpdate"|"newPermissions"|"appRestricionsSchemaChange"|"productAvailabilityChange"|"newDevice"|"deviceReportUpdate"|"enterpriseUpgrade"

---A resource returned by the PullNotificationSet API, which contains a collection of notifications for enterprises associated with the service account authenticated for the request.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.NotificationSet
---@field notificationSetId? string The notification set ID, required to mark the notification as received with the Enterprises.AcknowledgeNotification API. This will be omitted if no notifications are present.
---@field notification? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.NotificationList The notifications received, or empty if no notifications are present.

---Information about the current page. List operations that supports paging return only one "page" of results. This protocol buffer message describes the page that has been returned.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.PageInfo
---@field totalResults? number Total number of results available on the backend ! The total number of results in the result set.
---@field resultPerPage? number Maximum number of results returned in one page. ! The number of results included in the API response.
---@field startIndex? number Index of the first result returned in the current page.

---A Permissions resource represents some extra capability, to be granted to an Android app, which requires explicit consent. An enterprise admin must consent to these permissions on behalf of their users before an entitlement for the app can be created. The permissions collection is read-only. The information provided for each permission (localized name and description) is intended to be used in the MDM user interface when obtaining consent from the enterprise.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.Permission
---@field description? string A longer description of the Permissions resource, giving more details of what it affects.
---@field name? string The name of the permission.
---@field permissionId? string An opaque string uniquely identifying the permission.

---The device policy for a given managed device.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.Policy
---@field maintenanceWindow? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.MaintenanceWindow The maintenance window defining when apps running in the foreground should be updated.
---@field productPolicy? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyList The list of product policies. The productAvailabilityPolicy needs to be set to WHITELIST or ALL for the product policies to be applied.
---@field policyId? string An identifier for the policy that will be passed with the app install feedback sent from the Play Store.
---@field productAvailabilityPolicy? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.PolicyProductAvailabilityPolicyEnum|string The availability granted to the device for the specified products. "all" gives the device access to all products, regardless of approval status. "all" does not enable automatic visibility of "alpha" or "beta" tracks. "whitelist" grants the device access the products specified in productPolicy[]. Only products that are approved or products that were previously approved (products with revoked approval) by the enterprise can be whitelisted. If no value is provided, the availability set at the user level is applied by default.
---@field autoUpdatePolicy? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.PolicyAutoUpdatePolicyEnum|string Controls when automatic app updates on the device can be applied. Recommended alternative: autoUpdateMode which is set per app, provides greater flexibility around update frequency. When autoUpdateMode is set to AUTO_UPDATE_POSTPONED or AUTO_UPDATE_HIGH_PRIORITY, autoUpdatePolicy has no effect. - choiceToTheUser allows the device's user to configure the app update policy. - always enables auto updates. - never disables auto updates. - wifiOnly enables auto updates only when the device is connected to wifi. *Important:* Changes to app update policies don't affect updates that are in progress. Any policy changes will apply to subsequent app updates.
---@field deviceReportPolicy? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.PolicyDeviceReportPolicyEnum|string Whether the device reports app states to the EMM. The default value is "deviceReportDisabled".

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.PolicyAutoUpdatePolicyEnum "autoUpdatePolicyUnspecified"|"choiceToTheUser"|"never"|"wifiOnly"|"always"

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.PolicyDeviceReportPolicyEnum "deviceReportPolicyUnspecified"|"deviceReportDisabled"|"deviceReportEnabled"

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.PolicyProductAvailabilityPolicyEnum "productAvailabilityPolicyUnspecified"|"whitelist"|"all"

---A Products resource represents an app in the Google Play store that is available to at least some users in the enterprise. (Some apps are restricted to a single enterprise, and no information about them is made available outside that enterprise.) The information provided for each product (localized name, icon, link to the full Google Play details page) is intended to allow a basic representation of the product within an EMM user interface.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.Product
---@field requiresContainerApp? boolean Deprecated.
---@field appRestrictionsSchema? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.AppRestrictionsSchema The app restriction schema
---@field productPricing? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductProductPricingEnum Whether this product is free, free with in-app purchases, or paid. If the pricing is unknown, this means the product is not generally available anymore (even though it might still be available to people who own it).
---@field fullDescription? string The localized full app store description, if available.
---@field lastUpdatedTimestampMillis? string The approximate time (within 7 days) the app was last published, expressed in milliseconds since epoch.
---@field availableTracks? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductAvailableTracksItemEnumList Deprecated, use appTracks instead.
---@field appTracks? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.TrackInfoList The tracks visible to the enterprise.
---@field description? string The localized promotional description, if available.
---@field distributionChannel? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductDistributionChannelEnum How and to whom the package is made available. The value publicGoogleHosted means that the package is available through the Play store and not restricted to a specific enterprise. The value privateGoogleHosted means that the package is a private app (restricted to an enterprise) but hosted by Google. The value privateSelfHosted means that the package is a private app (restricted to an enterprise) and is privately hosted.
---@field detailsUrl? string A link to the (consumer) Google Play details page for the product.
---@field smallIconUrl? string A link to a smaller image that can be used as an icon for the product. This image is suitable for use at up to 128px x 128px.
---@field category? string The app category (e.g. RACING, SOCIAL, etc.)
---@field availableCountries? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.StringList The countries which this app is available in.
---@field permissions? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPermissionList A list of permissions required by the app.
---@field workDetailsUrl? string A link to the managed Google Play details page for the product, for use by an Enterprise admin.
---@field contentRating? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductContentRatingEnum The content rating for this app.
---@field screenshotUrls? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.StringList A list of screenshot links representing the app.
---@field title? string The name of the product.
---@field features? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductFeaturesItemEnumList Noteworthy features (if any) of this product.
---@field appVersion? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.AppVersionList App versions currently available for this product.
---@field recentChanges? string A description of the recent changes made to the app.
---@field signingCertificate? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductSigningCertificate The certificate used to sign this product.
---@field authorName? string The name of the author of the product (for example, the app developer).
---@field iconUrl? string A link to an image that can be used as an icon for the product. This image is suitable for use at up to 512px x 512px.
---@field minAndroidSdkVersion? number The minimum Android SDK necessary to run the app.
---@field productId? string A string of the form *app:<package name>*. For example, app:com.google.android.gm represents the Gmail app.

---An event generated when a product's approval status is changed.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductApprovalEvent
---@field productId? string The id of the product (e.g. "app:com.google.android.gm") for which the approval status has changed. This field will always be present.
---@field approved? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductApprovalEventApprovedEnum Whether the product was approved or unapproved. This field will always be present.

