---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPermissions
---@field permission? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPermissionList The permissions required by the app.
---@field productId? string The ID of the app that the permissions relate to, e.g. "app:com.google.android.gm".

---The policy for a product.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicy
---@field trackIds? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.StringList Grants the device visibility to the specified product release track(s), identified by trackIds. The list of release tracks of a product can be obtained by calling Products.Get.
---@field autoUpdateMode? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyAutoUpdateModeEnum|string The auto-update mode for the product. When autoUpdateMode is used, it always takes precedence over the user's choice. So when a user makes changes to the device settings manually, these changes are ignored.
---@field enterpriseAuthenticationAppLinkConfigs? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.EnterpriseAuthenticationAppLinkConfigList An authentication URL configuration for the authenticator app of an identity provider. This helps to launch the identity provider's authenticator app during the authentication happening in a private app using Android WebView. Authenticator app should already be the default handler for the authentication url on the device.
---@field autoInstallPolicy? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.AutoInstallPolicy The auto-install policy for the product.
---@field managedConfiguration? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ManagedConfiguration The managed configuration for the product.
---@field tracks? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyTracksItemEnumList Deprecated. Use trackIds instead.
---@field productId? string The ID of the product. For example, "app:com.google.android.gm".

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyAutoUpdateModeEnum "autoUpdateModeUnspecified"|"autoUpdateDefault"|"autoUpdatePostponed"|"autoUpdateHighPriority"

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyList gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicy[]

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyTracksItemEnum "appTrackUnspecified"|"production"|"beta"|"alpha"

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyTracksItemEnumList (gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductPolicyTracksItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductProductPricingEnum "unknown"|"free"|"freeWithInAppPurchase"|"paid"

---A set of products.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductSet
---@field productSetBehavior? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductSetProductSetBehaviorEnum The interpretation of this product set. "unknown" should never be sent and is ignored if received. "whitelist" means that the user is entitled to access the product set. "includeAll" means that all products are accessible, including products that are approved, products with revoked approval, and products that have never been approved. "allApproved" means that the user is entitled to access all products that are approved for the enterprise. If the value is "allApproved" or "includeAll", the productId field is ignored. If no value is provided, it is interpreted as "whitelist" for backwards compatibility. Further "allApproved" or "includeAll" does not enable automatic visibility of "alpha" or "beta" tracks for Android app. Use ProductVisibility to enable "alpha" or "beta" tracks per user.
---@field productId? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.StringList The list of product IDs making up the set of products.
---@field productVisibility? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductVisibilityList Additional list of product IDs making up the product set. Unlike the productID array, in this list It's possible to specify which tracks (alpha, beta, production) of a product are visible to the user. See ProductVisibility and its fields for more information. Specifying the same product ID both here and in the productId array is not allowed and it will result in an error.

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ProductSetProductSetBehaviorEnum "unknown"|"whitelist"|"includeAll"|"allApproved"

