---A service account identity, including the name and credentials that can be used to authenticate as the service account.
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ServiceAccount
---@field key? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ServiceAccountKey Credentials that can be used to authenticate as this ServiceAccount.
---@field name? string The account name of the service account, in the form of an email address. Assigned by the server.

--- *Deprecated:* New integrations cannot use this method and can refer to our new recommendations
---@class gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ServiceAccountKey
---@field publicData? string Public key data for the credentials file. This is an X.509 cert. If you are using the googleCredentials key type, this is identical to the cert that can be retrieved by using the X.509 cert url inside of the credentials file.
---@field data? string The body of the private key credentials file, in string format. This is only populated when the ServiceAccountKey is created, and is not stored by Google. When type is "pkcs12", the contents of the data field is base64 encoded and has the password "notasecret".
---@field id? string An opaque, unique identifier for this ServiceAccountKey. Assigned by the server.
---@field type? gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ServiceAccountKeyTypeEnum The file format of the generated key data.

---@alias gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ServiceAccountKeyList gcp.androidenterprise_v1.ServiceAccountKey[]

